    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter tonight\u2019s slate with **Yordan Alvarez** and **Pete Crow-Armstrong** serving as our primary offensive anchors. **Yordan Alvarez** (82.97) remains the clear-cut start of the day; his matchup against a favorable 5.23 xERA arm, combined with his elite .451 xwOBA, cements his floor. Similarly, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (80.98) is a priority play due to his lead-off positioning and a significant boost from dynamic platoon advantages against Junk. The scarcity of stolen bases remains our core philosophy, and **Christian Yelich** (75.84) earns an \"Elite\" designation today not just for his batting order placement, but because the slow delivery of Lowder creates a perfect environment for him to exploit the base paths, significantly outweighing other mid-tier options.\n\nWhile our starting nine remains robust, the most difficult decision involved keeping **Junior Caminero** (53.59) in the utility spot over our bench alternatives. Although **Junior Caminero** faces a stiff challenge against the 3.07 xERA of Williams, his base projection held up better than the restricted utility options. **Colt Keith** and **Dillon Dingler** were the closest to cracking the lineup, but both were penalized for unfavorable platoon splits against Griffin and a general lack of confirmed starting volume, essentially rendering them non-starters for our current game cap management strategy.\n\nRisks for today center on the top of the order. **Trea Turner** (55.24) faces an uphill battle against the veteran arm of Sale; despite the favorable order placement, his score is suppressed by the elite pitcher skill profile. We are also monitoring the remaining outfield rotation closely; while **Lars Nootbaar** (62.86) benefits from an aggressive dynamic platoon adjustment against Javier, **Carson Benge** (52.67) is effectively a marginal play, held back by a difficult platoon matchup against Wilkinson. We will keep **Josh Smith**, **Jacob Gonzalez**, **Hector Rodriguez**, **Luis Pena**, and **Pedro Ramirez** on standby in the farm system should late-breaking lineup changes force a pivot.",
